Title:
RustyWater ShellCode Dropper

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- Repository describing a Rust-based, multi-stage Windows dropper/payload (“reddit.exe” with a fake Cloudflare icon) associated with “RustyWater” and referenced as part of “Static Kitten” tradecraft.  
- It focuses on AV/EDR evasion via an 8-layer anti-analysis gate (sandbox/VM/debugger heuristics) before executing the real payload.  
- Persistence is implemented through Windows Registry Run keys with logic to fall back from HKLM to HKCU and verify the startup entry.  
- Execution is achieved through classic remote process injection into explorer.exe using VirtualAllocEx + WriteProcessMemory + CreateRemoteThread to run shellcode inside a trusted process.  
- The repo also documents staging via an intermediary “CertificationKit.ini” (actually a compiled Rust binary) that stores an XOR-encrypted payload, decrypts at runtime, and drops/executes it.  
- Useful for red teamers/malware developers studying common evasion + injection patterns, and for blue teams building detections around these behaviors.

Technical Focus:
- Anti-analysis / sandbox & VM artifact detection (CPU/RAM/uptime/user/MAC/process/registry checks)
- Windows Registry persistence (HKLM/HKCU Run keys, validation/fallback)
- Remote thread process injection into explorer.exe
- In-memory RWX allocation and shellcode execution (VirtualAllocEx, WriteProcessMemory, CreateRemoteThread)
- Simple payload obfuscation (XOR encryption) and staged dropper design
- PE metadata/resource editing for masquerading (rcedit)

Use Cases:
- Simulating commodity malware tradecraft in controlled red team exercises
- Building detection logic for anti-analysis checks and early-exit behavior
- Hunting for registry-based persistence and explorer.exe injection chains
- Malware analysis training on staged droppers with runtime decryption
- Creating YARA/Sigma/EDR analytics around suspicious WinAPI sequences and RWX allocations

Keywords:
Rust, Windows malware, dropper, shellcode, anti-analysis, sandbox evasion, VM detection, IsDebuggerPresent, registry persistence, HKLM Run, HKCU Run, explorer.exe injection, VirtualAllocEx, WriteProcessMemory, CreateRemoteThread, PROCESS_ALL_ACCESS, XOR encryption, staged payload, masquerading, rcedit